# rs-gf256-v1 known answers for the CultNet media FEC codec.
#
# Produced by reed-solomon-erasure 6.0.0 (galois_8; encode_sep, then
# reconstruct_data, which returned the original data for every pattern below),
# through generate_rs_gf256_v1_known_answers in tests/media_fec.rs at CultLib
# commit 73bf4421, before cultnet-rs replaced the crate with its own
# implementation of the construction documented in src/media_fec.rs.
# If these bytes ever change, rs-gf256-v1 changed meaning: bump the scheme id.
#
# case <k> <m> <shard_bytes> <fill>   a block of k data and m parity shards
#   fill lcg:  data shard i is bytes(k * 65536 + m * 256 + i, shard_bytes), where
#              bytes(seed, n) starts state = seed * 2654435761 + 1 and n times sets
#              state = state * 1664525 + 1013904223 and emits state >> 24, all
#              arithmetic on unsigned 32-bit integers, wrapping.
#   fill zero: every data byte is 0x00.  fill ff: every data byte is 0xff.
# parity <p> <hex>   parity shard p, lowercase hex
# erase <i,...>      a pattern of erased shards (0..k data, k..k+m parity); the
#                    shards left recover the erased data exactly
